ob to pitch  a longer version to shutter  an online streaming platform that  specializes in horror thrillers and  suspense  they loved the idea and he was off to  the races in fact there was a bidding  war for the movie since  nothing else could be made during the  lockdown there was just one problem  how do you film a movie at the height of  a pandemic  luckily the premise itself six friends  meeting over zoom to conduct a seance is  social distancing at its finest director  rob had the actors record their scenes  in dialogue and  with the help of experts in makeup and  stunts directed the actors on how to do  their own visual effects such as  moving the chair the actors lit the  scenes themselves  did their own makeup and operated their  own cameras while  rob directed them all from his own  apartment the story itself was based off  a 10-page treatment and they essentially  built it off the locations and crew they  had access to  for example rob had a special effects  makeup artist who hand crafted pieces of  latex  mailed them to the actress then got  online to instruct her on how to apply  the pieces to her face  his glitches like dan says yeah  one of the actresses was rooming with a  stunt coordinator so they were able to  utilize him to legally perform some of  the more dangerous stunts  the story even takes place during the  pandemic  we see one of the characters wearing a  mask the characters joke about social  distancing  and near the end two of the characters  elbow bump instead of shaking hands  all in all the film was shot in two  weeks and from initial idea to  distribution  it was an astonishingly short 12 weeks  now you might recognize  some of the actors in the film are  robb's actual friends who were in his  viral prank video  haley gemma carolyn emma and rodina  all star in the feature version now i  struggled to define it as a feature as  it's only  56 minutes long rob was contractually  obligated to deliver  an at least 30 minute long film and he  tinkered with the idea to make it a  real-time  40-minute call which is the time limit  for basic zoom meetings involving three  or more participants  now the film does manipulate time in  this respect stretching this 40 minutes  to 56 as seen at the ending  when the countdown to the remaining  meeting time is shown in the top left  corner but let's rewind to the beginning  host refers to haley the host of the  zoom meeting who takes off a piece of  tape on our webcam  as if the fbi or some stranger is  watching her little does she know that  someone will be watching her just not  someone from this world the group of six  friends are holding an online seance and  have been requested by their medium  salen to bring  items associated with the dead person  they'd like to connect with  for example teddy brings a creepy  ballerina music box that once belonged  to his grandmother  salen calls these trigger objects as  they may help in establishing a  connection with those who have passed  these spirits live in a place called the  astral plane which seems to be a place  existing between  our world and the next the film does a  great job at  pacing both the tension and scares for  example early on in the seance a creepy  knocking is heard only for us to  discover it's the medium's delivery guy  gemma then tells the group she feels  something in her room and  someone whispered the name jack to her  she tells everyone that jack was a nice  kid from school who once helped her when  she was a kid and he later hung himself  all of the girls are freaked out by  gemma's story but she soon reveals it  was  all a joke just like how rob played a  joke on his friends in his original  video this is the event that releases a  demonic spirit haley's chair is pushed  back  carolyn finds a pair of skinny legs in  her attic which disappear  emma's wine glass breaks on its own and  haley takes a polaroid to find what  appears to be an image of someone  hanging themselves  it's only when the group informed salem  that gemma's story about jack was made  up that we get a clearer picture of  what's going on  gemma has disrespected the spirits and  by inviting a person who doesn't exist  has someday quote false spirit according  to salem by  making something up you've essentially  created a mask so that anything  can come through and wear that mask it  could be something  even something demonic now there is a  scene later in the movie where the  spirit actually  levitates a mask which is likely a  callback to this  so essentially by gemma making up this  story of a boy named jack who hung  himself  she's invited a demonic spirit to  manifest and take control of that  made-up boy  that's why there are several references  to a noose in the film like  when teddy finds one in the barn or the  one found in haley's polaroid what  essentially follows is a series of  increasingly  paranormal events like the lights  turning on and off rodina's missing  boyfriend who collapses to the ground  seemingly out of nowhere and my personal  favorite teddy's girlfriend  levitating over the pool this one i  couldn't 100 confirm how they did but  considering the actor who plays teddy is  a professional stuntman and rigger  my guess is they actually set up a  device to lift her over the pool  now i gotta hand it to gemma who is one  of the final two survivors who ends up  running to her friend haley's house but  still manages to put on her mask  there she finds haley is still alive and  with a few remaining seconds left in  their zoom call  and yes they're still filming for some  reason they uncover the demon before  their session  ends this is the demon jack but on imdb  he's simply listed as the spirit the  film ends with the termination of their  zoom call and just a really cool  short and sweet end credit sequence the  credits are done as if all new members  were in the zoom call  plus you can make out the date july 30th  2020 which is the actual day the movie  was releas